# Migrate from InsForge to Supabase Auth

## Problem

InsForge's email verification returns `500 Failed to create verification token`, making user registration unusable. We're migrating to **Supabase Auth** which has reliable, built-in email delivery.

## Strategy

**Backend-only swap**: Replace the InsForge HTTP client with Supabase GoTrue API calls. The frontend API contract (`/api/v1/auth/*`) stays identical — **no frontend changes needed** except swapping env vars.

### Supabase Credentials
| Key | Value |
|-----|-------|
| Project Ref | `[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]` |
| URL | `https://[YOUR-PROJECT-REF].supabase.co` |
| Anon Key | `[YOUR_ANON_KEY]` |
| Service Role Key | `[YOUR_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY]` |
| Database | `postgresql://postgres:[PASSWORD]@db.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres` |

### API Mapping (InsForge → Supabase GoTrue)

| Function | InsForge | Supabase |
|----------|----------|----------|
| Register | `POST /api/auth/users` | `POST /auth/v1/signup` |
| Login | `POST /api/auth/sessions` | `POST /auth/v1/token?grant_type=password` |
| Validate session | `GET /api/auth/sessions/current` | `GET /auth/v1/user` |
| Send verification | `POST /api/auth/email/send-verification` | `POST /auth/v1/resend` (type=signup) |
| Verify OTP | `POST /api/auth/email/verify` | `POST /auth/v1/verify` (type=signup) |
| Send reset email | `POST /api/auth/email/send-reset-password` | `POST /auth/v1/recover` |
| Reset password | `POST /api/auth/email/reset-password` | `PUT /auth/v1/user` |
| Refresh token | `POST /api/auth/refresh` | `POST /auth/v1/token?grant_type=refresh_token` |
| Logout | `POST /api/auth/logout` | `POST /auth/v1/logout` |
| Admin list users | `GET /api/auth/users` | `GET /auth/v1/admin/users` |

## Proposed Changes

### Backend — Supabase Client

#### [MODIFY] [insforge_client.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/insforge_client.go) → rename to `supabase_client.go`

Replace the entire InsForge HTTP client with Supabase GoTrue API equivalents:
- `insforgeConfigured()` → `supabaseConfigured()` (reads `SUPABASE_URL` + `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`)
- `insforgePost()` → `supabasePost()` (calls Supabase GoTrue endpoints)
- `insforgePostEmailSendVerification()` → `supabaseResendVerification()` (uses service role key)
- `insforgeAdminConfigured()` → `supabaseServiceRoleConfigured()` (reads `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`)
- `insforgeAdminFindUserIDByEmail()` → `supabaseAdminFindUserIDByEmail()`
- All HTTP calls use `apikey` header instead of `x-api-key`

---

#### [MODIFY] [auth.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/auth.go)

Update session validation to call Supabase `GET /auth/v1/user` with Bearer token instead of InsForge `/api/auth/sessions/current`.

---

#### [MODIFY] [handlers.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/handlers.go)

Update all auth handlers to use Supabase API response shapes:
- `registerHandler`: Call Supabase signup, parse different response shape
- `loginHandler`: Call Supabase token endpoint
- `verifyEmailHandler`: Call Supabase verify endpoint
- `resendVerificationHandler`: Call Supabase resend endpoint
- `sendResetPasswordEmailHandler`: Call Supabase recover endpoint
- `resetPasswordHandler`: Call Supabase update user endpoint

---

#### [MODIFY] [handlers_insforge_extended.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/handlers_insforge_extended.go)

Update OAuth, refresh, logout, and profile handlers to use Supabase equivalents.

---

#### [MODIFY] [main.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/main.go)

Replace InsForge startup checks with Supabase checks. Log `supabase auth enabled (URL)`.

---

#### [MODIFY] [util.go](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/services/user-service/util.go)

Rename `insforgeLoginEmail()` → `supabaseLoginEmail()` and update any InsForge-specific helpers.

