### Infrastructure

#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/Dockerfile)

Replace InsForge env vars with Supabase equivalents in start.sh:
- `INSFORGE_BASE_URL` → `SUPABASE_URL`
- `INSFORGE_ANON_KEY` → `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- `INSFORGE_ADMIN_API_KEY` → `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`

---

#### [MODIFY] [.env.example](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/.env.example)

Update env var documentation.

---

### Frontend (minimal changes)

#### [MODIFY] [insforge.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Desktop/tayosaecosystem/src/lib/insforge.ts) → rename to `supabase.ts`

Replace `@insforge/sdk` with `@supabase/supabase-js`:
```typescript
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';
export const supabase = createClient(
  import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL,
  import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
);
```

> [!NOTE]
> The frontend auth pages (Login, Register, Verify, ForgotPassword) all use `platformApi.ts` which calls the backend API. Since the backend API contract stays the same, **no auth page changes are needed**.

---

